EVALUATION.md §13 (EVL-07): a literal; a value passed along keeps its origin; a default with
via the literal that omitted it, a literal inside a default staying a literal; a table entry
from its key to its body; a map key at its key; a spread with via the copied value; values
computed at the top and inside functions, with their stacks; a JSON value with its pointer; an
absent optional without default, loaded and written; an input has no value (§11.2); a literal
inside a lambda within a default is computed (review call e). A loaded `a:srv.note` is at its
field declaration too, the evaluator backing the decoder (orchestrator log, M3 W1 eval calls).
